For data protection, we utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to ensure that personal data is appropriately protected. We also have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers by default unless there is an explicit legal basis.

To further protect data, access control standards are enforced, including multi-factor authentication (MFA) with methods such as TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), ensuring only authorized personnel can access the system. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) design experience helps in managing user roles and permissions effectively.

Network security is maintained through architecture patterns like Zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth, along with the deployment of IDS/IPS systems for intrusion detection and prevention. Regular penetration testing, at least annually and post-major releases, by partners such as Synacktiv (France) and HN Security (Italy), helps identify vulnerabilities.

For audit and logging purposes, all queries are logged with immutability ensured through append-only logs with SHA-256 hash chaining, stored for 7 years. Real-time SIEM integration with tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM enables prompt detection of security incidents.

Demonstrating compliance involves maintaining our ISO 27001 certification, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, valid until 2026-11-30. Our Data Protection Officer (DPO) can be contacted at dpo@nexus-engineering.it for any GDPR-related queries. We also conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) when necessary, with an average duration of 3 weeks.

Lastly, having experience with regulatory frameworks such as RGPD/GDPR, EU AI Act, RGS v2 (ANSSI), SecNumCloud, NIS2 Directive, and eIDAS ensures that we are well-equipped to handle the compliance requirements for data protection and security.
